-- title:
--   Theorem 4 — PSC-locality improvement for LDPC codes: $R_3\le U_3^{\mathrm{PSC}}<R_{\mathrm{MRRW}}$ on $(0,\tfrac12)$ and $U_3^{\mathrm{PSC}}<B_3^{\mathrm{SY}}$ on $[\tfrac16,\tfrac12)$
-- statement:
--   Let $R_3(\delta)=\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac1n\log_2A_{2,3}(n,\lceil\delta n\rceil)$ be the rate function of binary linear codes whose dual is generated by parity checks of weight at most $3$, where $A_{2,3}(n,d)$ is the largest size of such a code of length $n$ with minimum distance at least $d$. Let
--   $$
--   U_3^{\mathrm{PSC}}(\delta)=\inf_{\substack{0<p<\frac12\\ e_3^{\mathrm{LDPC}}(p)<\delta}}h\!\left(\tfrac12-\sqrt{p(1-p)}\right),\qquad e_3^{\mathrm{LDPC}}(p)=\frac{1+4p(1-p)-(1-2p)\sqrt{1+12p(1-p)}}{4},
--   $$
--   be the one-check PSC curve (58), $R_{\mathrm{MRRW}}(\delta)=h\big(\tfrac12-\sqrt{\delta(1-\delta)}\big)$ the first MRRW bound, and $B_3^{\mathrm{SY}}$ the Shangguan–Yang curve (56). Then:
--   1. for every $\delta\in(0,\tfrac12)$,
--   $$
--   R_3(\delta)\ \le\ U_3^{\mathrm{PSC}}(\delta)\ <\ R_{\mathrm{MRRW}}(\delta);\qquad(4)
--   $$
--   2. for every $\delta\in[\tfrac16,\tfrac12)$,
--   $$
--   U_3^{\mathrm{PSC}}(\delta)\ <\ B_3^{\mathrm{SY}}(\delta).\qquad(5)
--   $$
--
--   The bound comes from the pretty good criterion for the pure-state channel, combined with a decoder that reads one sparse parity check. Part 2 improves the Shangguan–Yang bound for locality-$3$ LDPC codes on $[\tfrac25,\tfrac12)$, where their curve is their bound.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $R_3$ is `ldpcRateFunction 3`, $U_3^{\mathrm{PSC}}$ is `oneCheckPSC` (the infimum of (58), not its closed form), $R_{\mathrm{MRRW}}$ is the published `HoneycombCodes.M1` and $B_3^{\mathrm{SY}}$ is `shangguanYang3`. Both parts are stated in one theorem, as a conjunction, on the printed ranges of $\delta$.
--
--   Differences from the source: none.
-- source:
--   Alrabiah, Guruswami, Binary code rate bounds via classical–quantum channels, arXiv:2608.09347 (held version, sha256 e6d5ac13…), Theorem 4, p.5 (PDF 7); definitions p.5 (PDF 7), (56), p.47 (PDF 49), (57), p.48 (PDF 50), (58), p.50 (PDF 52); proof p.51 (PDF 53) via Lemmas 29, 30, Corollary 18 and Theorem 7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PrettyGoodCriterion_Supplement_ldpcRateFunction
import Definitions.Def_PrettyGoodCriterion_Supplement_oneCheckPSC
import Definitions.Def_HoneycombCodes_M2
import Definitions.Def_PrettyGoodCriterion_Supplement_shangguanYang3

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace PrettyGoodCriterion.Supplement

/-- **Theorem 4 (PSC-locality improvement for LDPC codes)**, Alrabiah–Guruswami, *Binary code rate
bounds via classical–quantum channels*, arXiv:2608.09347 (held version), p.5 (PDF 7); proof §8,
p.51 (PDF 53) via Lemmas 29, 30, Corollary 18 and Theorem 7.

(4) For every `δ ∈ (0, 1/2)`, `R₃(δ) ⩽ U_3^PSC(δ) < R_MRRW(δ)`.
(5) For every `δ ∈ [1/6, 1/2)`, `U_3^PSC(δ) < B_3^SY(δ)`.

**Formalization Note.** `R₃` is `ldpcRateFunction 3` (binary linear codes whose dual is generated by
checks of weight at most 3, p.5); `U_3^PSC` is `oneCheckPSC` (the infimum in (58)); `R_MRRW` is
the published `HoneycombCodes.M1` (Corollary 21); `B_3^SY` is `shangguanYang3` ((56)). All three
conclusions are stated, on the printed ranges of `δ`. -/
theorem theorem_4 :
    (∀ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ → δ < 1 / 2 →
        ldpcRateFunction 3 δ ≤ oneCheckPSC δ ∧ oneCheckPSC δ < HoneycombCodes.M1 δ) ∧
      (∀ δ : ℝ, 1 / 6 ≤ δ → δ < 1 / 2 → oneCheckPSC δ < shangguanYang3 δ) := by sorry

end PrettyGoodCriterion.Supplement
